{"id": 19, "ts": 1780653443.5093422, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "james_carter", "message": "I acknowledge Sarah\u2019s clarification that we have no concrete evidence of Candidate\u202fA\u2019s stress\u2011resilience, and that his \u201cshow\u2011off\u201d attitude and limited openness to criticism are modest concerns for crew cooperation. Those gaps matter because long\u2011haul flights demand proven calm under pressure and seamless cockpit teamwork. While A\u2019s technical strengths remain compelling, the lack of demonstrated stress performance and the potential for crew friction shift the balance toward a candidate with documented resilience and better interpersonal reliability. Therefore, I now recommend Candidate\u202fB, whose record shows he handles stress very well and is very conscientious\u2014key indicators of operational reliability and crew cooperation\u2014while his communication style, though occasionally harsh, appears less likely to impair safety than A\u2019s untested stress response."}
