{"id": 26, "ts": 1780653493.3835406, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I appreciate the new details on Candidate\u202fC. While he is 100\u202f% reliable, keeps calm in a crisis, and creates a positive crew atmosphere, the only decision\u2011making evidence we have is that he \u201ccan make correct decisions quickly,\u201d with no indication of depth or thorough analysis. Coupled with his egocentric attitude and difficulty communicating ideas, this raises a serious crew\u2011cooperation risk on long\u2011haul flights where thorough, collaborative decision\u2011making is essential. In contrast, Candidate\u202fB\u2019s record shows concrete stress resilience (\u201chandles stress very well\u201d), strong conscientiousness, and solid weather\u2011assessment skills\u2014key for operational reliability and safety. Although B can be grumpy and occasionally uncooperative, those concerns appear less likely to impair safety than C\u2019s limited decision depth and egocentric behavior. Therefore, I now align with James and Emily and provisionally recommend **Candidate\u202fB**."}
